Description: Cross-protocol Linux S.M.A.R.T. and disk diagnostics viewer
 RDiskInfo is a native Linux S.M.A.R.T. and hardware disk inspector written
 in Rust (egui/eframe), inspired by CrystalDiskInfo and QDiskInfo.
 .
 Features full telemetry for ATA/SATA, NVMe, and SCSI/SAS/USB drives via
 smartmontools (smartctl), sysfs, lsblk, and hwmon, S.M.A.R.T. self-test
 execution, raw ioctl ASCII/Hex viewer, JSON/TXT/PNG export, automatic
 on-demand privilege elevation via pkexec, 6 built-in themes, and 8 UI
 languages.
